note OM-1 twin of rot-values.om (contract section 3 lines 76-83), for the pinned compiler 734f0a39:
note the same computation with rotations written as OM-1 shifts (tr*/tl* below: n = 0 returns x, else
note or shr x n shl x w-n; OMEGESE 9.3: unsigned shl wraps modulo 2^w, shift amounts 0..w-1).
note Same expected stdout as the OM-2 unit: oracle/s3s4/exp/rot-values.out. This cross-checks the
note python oracle against OM-1 arithmetic now, independent of any OM-2 compiler.
note (this line replaces the om2 line, so the line numbers equal those of rot-values.om)
note OM-1 unit
fn rr8 x uchar n uchar to uchar
ret tr8 x n
end
fn rl8 x uchar n uchar to uchar
ret tl8 x n
end
fn rr16 x ushort n ushort to ushort
ret tr16 x n
end
fn rl16 x ushort n ushort to ushort
ret tl16 x n
end
fn rr32 x uint n uint to uint
ret tr32 x n
end
fn rl32 x uint n uint to uint
ret tl32 x n
end
fn rr64 x ulong n ulong to ulong
ret tr64 x n
end
fn rl64 x ulong n ulong to ulong
ret tl64 x n
end
fn main to int
a = uchar 177
pu ulong tr8 a 0
pu ulong tr8 a 1
pu ulong tr8 a 3
pu ulong tr8 a 7
pu ulong tl8 a 0
pu ulong tl8 a 1
pu ulong tl8 a 3
pu ulong tl8 a 7
pu ulong rr8 a 0
pu ulong rr8 a 1
pu ulong rr8 a 3
pu ulong rr8 a 7
pu ulong rl8 a 0
pu ulong rl8 a 1
pu ulong rl8 a 3
pu ulong rl8 a 7
for n uchar 8
pu ulong rr8 a n
pu ulong rl8 a n
end
b = ushort 45508
pu ulong tr16 b 0
pu ulong tr16 b 1
pu ulong tr16 b 5
pu ulong tr16 b 15
pu ulong tl16 b 0
pu ulong tl16 b 1
pu ulong tl16 b 5
pu ulong tl16 b 15
pu ulong rr16 b 0
pu ulong rr16 b 1
pu ulong rr16 b 5
pu ulong rr16 b 15
pu ulong rl16 b 0
pu ulong rl16 b 1
pu ulong rl16 b 5
pu ulong rl16 b 15
for n ushort 16
pu ulong rr16 b n
pu ulong rl16 b n
end
c = uint 4041331395
pu ulong tr32 c 0
pu ulong tr32 c 1
pu ulong tr32 c 13
pu ulong tr32 c 31
pu ulong tl32 c 0
pu ulong tl32 c 1
pu ulong tl32 c 13
pu ulong tl32 c 31
pu ulong rr32 c 0
pu ulong rr32 c 1
pu ulong rr32 c 13
pu ulong rr32 c 31
pu ulong rl32 c 0
pu ulong rl32 c 1
pu ulong rl32 c 13
pu ulong rl32 c 31
for n uint 32
pu ulong rr32 c n
pu ulong rl32 c n
